# PyTorch Patterns

## Device Handling

Always resolve device once and pass it explicitly — never hardcode `"cuda"` or `"cpu"`:

```python
device = torch.device("cuda" if torch.cuda.is_available() else "mps" if torch.backends.mps.is_available() else "cpu")
model = model.to(device)
x = x.to(device)
```

## Training Loop

Prefer explicit train/eval mode toggling:

```python
model.train()
for batch in train_loader:
    optimizer.zero_grad()
    loss = criterion(model(x), y)
    loss.backward()
    optimizer.step()

model.eval()
with torch.no_grad():
    val_loss = criterion(model(x_val), y_val)
```

## Checkpointing

Save the full training state so runs are resumable:

```python
torch.save({
    "epoch": epoch,
    "model_state_dict": model.state_dict(),
    "optimizer_state_dict": optimizer.state_dict(),
    "loss": loss,
}, "checkpoints/run_{run_name}_epoch{epoch}.pt")
```

## Shape Comments

Add shape comments on tensor operations when the shapes aren't obvious:

```python
# x: (B, T, C) — batch, sequence length, embedding dim
x = self.attn(x)  # (B, T, C)
```

## No Silent Failures

Never catch broad exceptions around forward passes. Let shape mismatches crash loudly.
